course: dictionary
lesson: 5334
title: Kilograms and kg
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Kg is the short way to write kilogram. A kilogram is a unit for how heavy something is. When you read «An adult head weighs about 5 kg», the 5 kg tells you how heavy the head is, the same way 5 cm tells you how long something is.
explain: Kg is the same for one or for many. You write 1 kg and you also write 5 kg, 20 kg or 100 kg. The letters never change to add an s.
explain: One kilogram is 1000 grams, so a kilogram is much heavier than a gram. «A giraffe's heart weighs about 11 kg» means the heart weighs about 11 000 grams. To change kg into g, multiply by 1000.
explain: You meet kg at the shop, at the airport and in science. Fruit and flour are often sold by the kilogram, and prices can be given «per kg». In science, a bag of sugar is about 1 kg, and mass is measured in kilograms.
fact: Kg is short for kilogram, a unit of mass.
fact: 1 kg is 1000 grams.
fact: Kg stays the same for one or many: 1 kg, 5 kg, 100 kg.
fact: «A giraffe's heart weighs about 11 kg.» That is about the weight of a small child.
fact: «Per kg» means for each kilogram, as in a price of £2 per kg.
fact: To change kg into g, multiply by 1000. So 2 kg is 2000 g.
exercise: What does kg stand for? | *kilogram | gram | kilowatt | kilometre
exercise: «The harpy eagle can weigh up to about 9 kg.» How many grams is that? | 900 g | 90 g | *9000 g | 9 g
exercise: Which weighs more: 1 kg or 500 g? | *1 kg | 500 g | They weigh the same
test: «An elephant calf weighs about 100 kg.» How many grams is that? | 1000 g | *100 000 g | 10 g | 10 000 g
test: Apples cost £2 «per kg». What does «per kg» mean? | for one bag only | for the whole shop | for each gram | *for each kilogram
exam: Lily has a 2 kg bag of apples and a 500 g bag of plums. How many grams altogether? | 2050 g | 250 g | *2500 g | 25 g
